-- Driver Question Bank — expands driver_probe_questions (migration 106)
-- from 7 rows to 87, covering the 33 drivers in MEF-driver-library-v1.md
-- that get daily questions (MEC-2/MEC-3 are camera-assessment-only, per
-- that doc, and correctly get none). Content drafted in
-- docs/driver-question-bank-draft-v1.md, corrected there by the site
-- owner before this migration was written — every prompt/option label
-- below is taken verbatim from that file.
--
-- 1. Adds `screen` ('morning' | 'evening') to driver_probe_questions —
--    which of the two existing check-in surfaces (Morning Readiness,
--    Evening Reflection) a question belongs on. This was previously an
--    unwritten convention (each screen's React component hard-coded which
--    exact question_keys it recognized); making it a real column is what
--    lets a future question be routed to the right screen with a plain
--    update, no deploy — the same "no deploy" property this table
--    already had for a question's existence, now extended to its
--    placement too.
-- 2. Backfills `screen` for the 7 existing rows to match their CURRENT,
--    already-shipped behavior exactly (see app/checkin/CheckinForm.tsx
--    and app/checkin/evening/EveningReflectionForm.tsx as they stood
--    before this migration) — nothing about where an existing question
--    appears changes.
-- 3. Wires morning_soreness (an existing daily_checkins column, asked
--    unconditionally on Morning Readiness since migration 63, never
--    previously linked to a driver) to MOV-5 — pure backend evidence
--    wiring for the driver-state engine, zero UI change, since that
--    field's own rendering was never gated by driver_probe_questions
--    membership.
-- 4. Inserts 80 new rows (docs/driver-question-bank-draft-v1.md's items
--    1-46 and 48-81; its item 47 is the morning_soreness wiring above,
--    not a new question). New goal-relevant follow-ups (e.g.
--    "what kept you up", "which meal(s) did you skip") reuse this same
--    table's existing `driver_id: null` local-follow-up convention
--    (established by migration 106's pain_location/pain_aggravating_factor
--    rows) — excluded from the server-side adaptive bank
--    (lib/daily-checkin-adaptive/probeBank.ts already skips any row with
--    a null driver_id), shown instead by client-side evaluation of their
--    own `requires` array against this same day's already-entered
--    answers (see components/checkin/DriverProbeField.tsx and the two
--    check-in forms, changed in the same commit as this migration).
alter table driver_probe_questions
  add column screen text not null default 'morning' check (screen in ('morning', 'evening'));

update driver_probe_questions set screen = 'evening'
where question_key in ('checkin_probe.digestion_rating', 'checkin_probe.movement_today');
-- night_waking_count, night_sweats, bowel_movement_status, pain_location,
-- pain_aggravating_factor keep the 'morning' default — matches their
-- current, unchanged rendering on Morning Readiness.


